Let \( S \) be a set of rational numbers satisfying the following conditions:
(1) If \( a \in S \) and \( b \in S \), then \( a+b \in S \) and \( ab \in S \);
(2) For any rational number \( r \), exactly one of the three statements \( r \in S \), \( -r \in S \), \( r = 0 \) holds. Prove that \( S \) is the set of all positive rational numbers.

